# GitHub auto-sync

After making any code or content changes in this repository:

1. Stage all relevant changes (`git add -A`).
2. Commit with a clear, concise message describing what changed and why.
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`).

Do not leave work only on disk. If push fails, tell the user immediately and include the error.

Remote: `https://github.com/AshPerry1/SPCG.git`

Project hooks in `.cursor/hooks.json` also debounce-commit-push after file edits and when the agent stops. Prefer explicit commit messages when you are the one editing; hooks use auto-sync messages as a backup.
